<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:svg="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:db="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.0-subset Scilab" xml:lang="en" xml:id="dtn_get_connectivity"><info><pubdate>November 2005</pubdate></info><refnamediv><refname>dtn_get_connectivity</refname><refpurpose> Get the connectivity of dtn</refpurpose></refnamediv>
	
   
	
   
	
   
	
   
	
   
	
   <refsynopsisdiv><title>Calling Sequence</title><synopsis>tes = dtn_get_connectivity(ptr);</synopsis></refsynopsisdiv>
	
   <refsection><title>Parameters</title>
		
      <variablelist>
			
         <varlistentry>
				
            <term>ptr</term>
				
            <listitem>
					: is a pointer representing dtn.
				</listitem>
			
         </varlistentry>
			
         <varlistentry>
				
            <term>tes</term>
				
            <listitem>
					: is a (nbsimplices,dcur+1) array where each row contains the indices of the vertices of the corresponding simplex, where dcur is the affine dimension of a set of points witch ptr is computed from, and nbsimplices is the number of simplices.
				</listitem>
			
         </varlistentry>
		
      </variablelist>
	
   </refsection>
	
   <refsection><title>Description</title>
		
      <para>
			Given a pointer ptr of dtn, tri = dtn_get_connectivity (ptr) allows to get the connectivity of dtn.
		</para>
	
   </refsection>
	
   <refsection><title>Examples</title><programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
x = rand(1,10);
y = rand(1,10);
points=[x' y'];
[tri,ptr] = delaunay_n(points);
new_x = rand(1,10);
new_y = rand(1,10);
new_points=[new_x' new_y']
dtn_insert_points(ptr,new_points);
new_tri = dtn_get_connectivity(ptr);
dtn_delete(ptr,"ptr");
new_tri
]]></programlisting></refsection>
	
